  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forest Landscape Restoration in Central America and the Caribbean and implementation of the Green Development Fund for Central America (REDD Landscape)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project enables private and public sector actors in selected influence areas of the Five Great Forests of Mesoamerica to jointly implement forest landscape restoration and deforestation-free land use forms including the creation of market-based incentives for landowners and primary sector producers. It promotes the establishment of public and private traceability systems for deforestation risk commodities, propels the creation of public-private alliances along strategic supply chains and aids in establishing zero deforestation jurisdictions with the participation of key stakeholders at the territorial level and along strategic supply chains, including indigenous groups and women-led organizations. International exchange and regional policy reform will be promoted via established integration mechanisms of the Central American region, global initiatives related with the UN Decade on Ecosystem Restoration and the EU Regulation on deforestation-free value chains.</narrative>
  </description>
